            4:43
            Mins | It's really rather good // 4.0 // 10 Nov. 2015 // By

    JB

TOP 100 REVIEWER on 10 Nov. 2015 // I got a free sample of this to review.The packaging it comes in is nice, though I did notice that everything in the box could easily have fit into something less than half the size. I am not a big fan of boxes too big for the contents, but at least the box looks nice, something moving about inside it will make it more exciting before unwrapping it as a gift, and so it's not all bad.Inside are the three different colours of sand and some moulds to play with, moulds that could of course just as easily be used with regular sand or other things.The play sand doesn't really feel like sand, but like a cross between saw dust and plasticine, not an entirely unpleasant feeling, really, and they are easy to work with, crumbling like sand sometimes, and sticking together like plasticine when you compress them properly.Using one of the moulds, the shape held rather well, though it did collapse a little bit on one of the ridges on the side. Still, an impressive result, I think, for something like this.After using it, there was a little bit of sand dust that I'd not managed to get back in the bag, but whatever causes the sand to stick together doesn't feel as if it leaves any residue on neither hands or work surface. Another good result, I think.Had I still been a child, I would have thought this was great fun – well, I still think it's great fun, to be honest. It is something that has a lot of potential for creativity while avoiding being too messy. | A fun set // 4.0 // 10 Dec. 2015 // By

    Sophie

TOP 1000 REVIEWER on 10 Dec. 2015 // My daughters (aged 8 & 5) have really enjoyed playing with this kinetic sand. The sand flows easily but when compressed it will retain its shape whether through using the three supplied moulds or their hands. They have even decided to use their collection of play doh moulds and cutters to great effect.I have found it is best to use the sand on a large tray because it does tend to get dropped on the floor / carpet. The bigger lumps are easy to pick up and the smaller pieces can often be collected by tapping them with bigger pieces, but it's almost inevitable that the vacuum cleaner will need an outing at the end of play.  That in itself is not a problem but it does mean that each time the sand is used a small amount is wasted.The sand supplied with this kit is in bags that have to be cut open so we have transferred the sand to zip lock bags and that works well. However, much like the afore mentioned play doh eventually it all gets mixed together and ends up as a lovely brown, so at the minute we have four bags of sand.In terms of use I find that ensuring the girls have clean dry hands is the best way to stop and sand sticking to their skin. I have also found it useful to have a soft paint brush to clean the play doh moulds to recover all of the sand.So there we are: it's better in many ways than play doh because it's easier to clean up and it doesn't set rock hard if left exposed to the air. I have to say I was surprised just how much my daughters like playing with this sand and it holds an edge very well so it is possible to produce some very lovely creations that only children can.Please note this sand was sent to me for review purposes. | Mess free fun for children // 5.0 // 6 Dec. 2015 // By

    niki

HALL OF FAMETOP 50 REVIEWER on 6 Dec. 2015 // Disclaimer: I received this product for a discount in exchange for an unbiased review.The packaging is quite large and colourful – but I would say slightly generous with its claims for the product inside. The box is a bit bigger than it needs to be to hold three light packs of play sand, three (green, for me) moulds and a container which for me was actually an almost broken plastic tray which got pushed aside and replaced straight away.The coloured play sand itself is a fun gift for any young child – with three reasonably sized packs of yellow, green and pink sand enough to keep kids entertained for a while. The different coloured sands inevitably mix together but that’s to be expected and surprisingly, any mess on the floor or surfaces are easy to clean off. The sand is easy to mould and manipulate as it is soft and sticky, but not to the level that it’s too sticky to use – hours of fun! The shapes once they come out of the three moulds last well and are worthwhile – though they’re only likely to be used once and then forgotten about. Overall, the set, though a little on the small side, is creative and fun and makes a pretty nice present.

